Next: wire strategy selection, snapshots, reconciliation, initial offsets and Push triggers; P11-V02/U01 remain open.

P11 reconciliation follow-up: compared `PushConsumer::rebalance_once` with pinned Java `RebalanceImpl.rebalanceByTopic`. Local clustering now looks up membership before handling a missing route and emits Java's empty-set queue callback for non-retry topics while preserving the previous assignment. Available empty routes still reach the allocator. Broker assignment queries no longer depend on the local route table. `LiteSelective` now follows Java's default no-op branch pending Phase 13 POP handling. Added `missing_clustering_route_queries_membership_notifies_empty_and_keeps_assignment` and `lite_selective_rebalance_leaves_assignments_for_pop_handling`.

P11 race-coverage follow-up: added `queue_removal_fences_a_pull_response_already_in_flight`, using barriers to hold a returned pull response until the queue generation has been dropped and safely removed. The response is rejected without changing offsets or queue contents.

